\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Be with us, gracious Lord, to- day,
\par This house we dedicate to Thee:
\par O hear Thy servants as they pray,
\par And let Thine ear attentive be!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Within these walls let holy peace,
\par Let love and truth be always found;
\par May burdened hearts find sweet release,
\par And souls with richest grace  be crowwned.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. May here be heard the suppliant's sigh,
\par The weary enter into rest;
\par Here may  the contrite to Thee cry;
\par And waiting souls be richly blessed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Here, when the gospel sound is heard,
\par And here proclaimed the saving name,
\par May hearts be quickened, moved, 
\par and stirred,
\par And souls be kindled into flame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Here may the dead be made to live;
\par The dumb to sing, the deaf to hear;
\par And do Thou to the humble give
\par Pardon and peace instead of fear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Make this, O Lord, Thine own abode;
\par Thy presence in these courts be given;
\par Be this, indeed, the house of God,
\par And this in truth the gate of Heaven.
\par                                          Amen. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

